idate B (as per SMM). We need to consider the new info: B has weak memory for numbers, no info on decision quality, feedback handling, adaptability. That is a concern. We also have notes on Candidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. Also we have note that C puts concern for others above everything (crew cooperation positive). Also C has excellent attention skills (attention). But communication difficulty and egocentric may affect crew cooperation. Also not willing to further education may affect adaptability.\n\nCandidate D: takes responsibility seriously, solves problems extremely well, can concentrate very well, responds to unexpected events adequately, moody, loner, know-it-all, hot temper. No explicit info on stress resilience, but we have \"responds to unexpected events adequately\" maybe indicates some stress resilience. But concerns about moody, loner, hot temper may affect crew cooperation and professional communication.\n\nCandidate A: anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, unfriendly, eats unhealthily. No info on stress resilience, crew cooperation, communication, reliability.\n\nWe need to discuss perhaps Candidate C as alternative, given his quick decision making and excellent attention skills, and crew positive attitude (puts concern for others). But communication difficulty and egocentric may be concerns.\n\nWe could argue that while B has strong reliability and stress resilience, the weak memory for numbers is a serious issue for attention and information accuracy. Since we have no evidence on decision quality, we cannot be confident. Candidate C has excellent attention skills and quick correct decisions, which directly addresses decision quality and attention, and his concern for others suggests good crew cooperation. However his communication difficulty and egocentric nature may be concerns. But perhaps overall C may be a better fit given the missing data for B.\n\nWe need to decide whether to keep vote for B or shift to C. We need to reference discussion: Agent 1 says still leaning B but wants more info. Agent 2 raised concerns about B and suggested D as alternative. We have not yet discussed C. So we can bring C into discussion, compare with B, and maybe adjust recommendation.\n\nGiven the evidence: B: strong reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, but weak memory for numbers, unknown decision quality, adaptability. C: quick correct decisions, excellent attention skills, puts concern for others (crew cooperation), but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). Which is stronger overall? The role requires reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention accuracy, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility, adaptability. B lacks evidence on decision quality and adaptability, and has weak memory. C has strong decision quality (quick correct decisions) and excellent attention, and crew positive, but lacks evidence on stress resilience and reliability. We have no info on C's reliability or stress resilience. That is a gap. So both have gaps.\n\nWe could argue that we need more info on C's stress resilience and reliability before shifting. So maybe keep B but note we need more info on both B and C. Or we could propose to gather info on C's stress resilience and reliability. Since we have no info, we could ask other agents for that.\n\nThus our contribution: I agree with Agent 1 that B is still provisional but we need more info on decision quality and adaptability. I propose we now bring Candidate C into discussion, highlighting his quick correct decisions and excellent attention, and ask for any observations on his stress resilience, reliability, and crew cooperation. This will help compare.\n\nWe need to state our current recommendation: still Candidate B, but we are open to shift pending new evidence. Provide reasoning.\n\nThus public message: I agree with Agent 1 that B remains provisional, but note the weak memory for numbers is a red flag for attention. I suggest we examine C's quick decision making and attention skills as a possible alternative, and request info on C's stress resilience and reliability. My vote remains B for now.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B."}
